    689				     ;------------------------------
    690				     ;## Part 2: Reading a 512-Byte Sector
    691				     ;Once the LBA target is specified,we issue	the Read Sectors Command (020)
    692				     ;to the Command Register. The drive will pull its Busy flag high,seek the
    693				     ;data internally,and then lower Busy while	raising	the DRQ	(Data Request)
    694				     ;flag to inform the Z80 that the 512-byte buffer is ready to be transferred.
    695				     ;This routine expects DI to point to the destination memory buffer	in your
    696				     ;Z80's RAM.
    697
    698				     ; =====================================================================
    699				     ; SUBROUTINE: IDE_READ_SECTOR
    700				     ; Inputs: DI = RAM	Destination Address for	the 512	bytes
    701				     ; Outputs:	Carry Flag set on Error,cleared	on Success
    702				     ; Destroys: A,BX,DI
